<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Vala State</h1><p class="st-meta">1740 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Vallabhipur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Gohil Rajput state in eastern Kathiawar whose capital stood on the ruins of Valabhi, the great early medieval city of the Maitrakas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Vala was founded around 1740 by a junior branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gohil">Gohil Rajputs</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhavnagar-state">Bhavnagar State</a>. Its town, Vala or Vallabhipur, lay at the site of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valabhi">Valabhi</a>, capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maitraka-dynasty">Maitraka</a> kingdom and a renowned Buddhist and Jain centre of learning.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Thakor ruled a modest agricultural territory within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar-agency">Kathiawar Agency</a>. Few details of the state's internal history are recorded; the site is better known for the excavations and inscriptions of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valabhi">Valabhi</a> than for its 18th and 19th century rulers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Vala was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948; it now lies in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhavnagar-state">Bhavnagar</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/vala-state.jpg" alt="Vala State" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Vala_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1740 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vallabhipur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vallabhipur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1844&amp;focus=vala-state" aria-label="Vala State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6610 1370 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vala State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6930 1626L7364 1601M6930 1626L7364 1602M6930 1626L6896 1610"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6896 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6930 1626h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6930 1626h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1844&amp;focus=vala-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
